# K-028 — snapshot PIT window sufficiency and freshness

1. 114 copies of ONE 1h bar, minimum_bars=100
   state/class      = 'VALID' / 'Q1'
   mtf_states       = {'1h': 'ALIGNED'}
   overall_mtf      = 'ALIGNED'
   observation_windows['1h'] = {'start': 1672124399999, 'end': 1672534799999, 'timeframe': '1h', 'bars': 114}
   distinct open times in the input = 1

2. the same call with a 1-second freshness_threshold on a 2023 bar
   state/class      = 'VALID' / 'Q1'
   identical snapshot_id as case 1 = True
   occurrences of 'freshness_threshold' in the function body = 1 (the signature parameter only)

3. 114 DISTINCT consecutive bars (the honest window)
   state/class      = 'VALID' / 'Q1'
   distinct open times = 114
   -> cases 1 and 3 are reported identically apart from as_of/hash

4. the PIT loop (apex/quality/pit.py:79-82)
   as_of_ms = max(availability) over the same list it then compares against, so `_availability_ms(obs) > as_of_ms` is unreachable: PIT_VIOLATION cannot be returned by this helper.
